From: Sobs <antohasobne@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:43:52 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 16/17] Dynamic resolution of the 3D view (BFG's resolution
 scaling, wired up)

When frames are slow, FullscreenFXManager::Process draws the player's
view cropped to a smaller size (CropRenderSize: the front end computes
viewport, light scissors and window coordinates for it), captures it
into the image _scaledSceneImage and stretches it over the screen with
the material _scaledScene (opaque; translucent so it is not depth
tested EQUAL in the 2D view). The HUD, texts and menus drawn after it
stay at the full size.

rs_enable 4: both axes alike; rs_minimum: the smallest scale. Without
GPU timer queries (Mesa: off in RBDOOM, and panfrost's split batches)
idResolutionScale::SetCurrentFrameTime steers by the time between
frames: it drops proportionally when frames take rs_frameDropMilliseconds
longer than the engine's rate, and rises a step after waiting at the
full rate, waiting longer after a rise that had to be taken back.

Handhelds: rs_enable 4, rs_minimum 0.6. Mali-G52 (854x480): the start of
mars_city2 27.8 -> 46 fps, the mars_city1 hangar 34 -> 54 fps; light
scenes keep the full size at 60 fps.
